# FamCart Admin configuration. Copy to .env and fill in.
#
# Everything here is a PUBLISHABLE key: the same values FamCart itself ships in
# its client bundle. That is deliberate and it is what makes this tool safe to
# build as a plain SPA. The admin dashboard reads cross-household data through
# `security definer` RPCs that check public.admin_users server-side, so holding
# these values gets an ordinary account exactly what an ordinary account already
# has: its own households and nothing else.
#
# There is NO service-role key here, and there must never be one. If a panel
# seems to need it, the answer is another RPC in FamCart's 008_admin.sql, not a
# secret in a browser.

# ─── the two app databases ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FamCart has two projects with IDENTICAL schemas and very different
# consequences: `famcart` holds real households, `famcart-dev` holds whatever was
# last tried. Configure both and the topbar grows a switcher; configure one and
# it is simply the project you are on, with no switcher and no ambiguity.
#
# The project ref is parsed out of each URL and shown on every screen, and
# production is marked in red wherever it appears. Development is the default
# when both are present, and switching TO production asks for confirmation --
# you need to be told when a mistake is expensive, not when it is cheap.
VITE_PROD_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-production-project.supabase.co
VITE_PROD_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

VITE_DEV_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-development-project.supabase.co
VITE_DEV_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ─── the product catalog ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The THIRD Supabase project, in its own organisation, shared live by production
# and development alike. It holds the imported and curated reference rows and
# nothing that belongs to a household.
#
# There is only one, so it does NOT switch with the app project. A switch changes
# every household number on screen and leaves every product number where it was,
# and the switcher says so rather than leaving you to notice.
#
# Optional. Leave both blank and the Products and Product Pipeline sections
# report the catalog as not configured rather than failing; every other section
# is unaffected. That mirrors how FamCart itself treats an absent catalog.
VITE_CATALOG_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_CATALOG_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ─── auth ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The same Clerk instance FamCart uses, which is what makes one signed-in session
# able to query both projects: all three name that issuer in their Third-Party
# Auth settings, so the token verifies everywhere.
#
# It is a pk_test_ key against a development instance, on purpose and permanently.
# See FamCart's CLAUDE.md for why that is the accepted state and not a finding.
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_

# ─── seeding, for local development only ──────────────────────────────────────
# There are no seed variables. famcart-dev is nearly empty, which leaves most of
# this dashboard rendering empty states; scripts/seed-dev.sql fills it with a
# plausible ninety days so every panel, chart and pager can be exercised.
#
# It is SQL rather than a script with a service-role key, deliberately: a key
# that can write every row should not need to exist in a second place just to
# make development data. Run it in the SQL editor of the project you mean, and
# read the guard at the top of the file first.
